-- No sequence is required.
--
-- REQUEST_ID is generated by the application (req- plus a UUID) and is the primary
-- key. Creating a database sequence would add a serialization point on the insert
-- path without giving the API a value it uses.
--
-- INGESTED_AT uses DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP. There is no surrogate numeric key.
--
-- This script is intentionally a successful no-op so installation automation can
-- run every file in order.

SET DEFINE ON
WHENEVER SQLERROR EXIT SQL.SQLCODE
DEFINE schema_owner = FMSPRD6

PROMPT No sequences are created for &schema_owner..MSISDN_ELIGIBILITY_AUDIT.
PROMPT Request identifiers are generated by the application and stored in REQUEST_ID.
